[2025-11-06 18:28:00 UTC]
FOLLOW-UP: Additional Async Integration Failures

OBSERVED REGRESSIONS (post-agent run):
  1. Synchronous bridge modules still call get_manager()
     • app/apps/file_editor_cm6/agent_bridge.py:425 (`self.manager = _manager()`) assigns the coroutine returned by async get_manager to self.manager. Any later call to `self.manager.spawn_shell(...)` now fails.
     • app/apps/file_editor_cm6/agent_bridge_mcp.py:416 uses the same pattern, so Codex MCP sessions break.
     • app/apps/terminal/backend.py defines `mgr()` returning `_manager()`. Every route now calls async methods (`list_shells`, `describe`, `spawn_shell_pty`) without awaiting them, so the entire terminal-backend API raises TypeError/RuntimeError on first use.

  2. agent_routes.py still wraps async methods in to_thread
     • get_agent_shell_status() calls `await anyio.to_thread.run_sync(mgr.list_shells)` even though `mgr.list_shells` is now async. Passing a coroutine into run_sync raises immediately, so the status endpoint is broken.

REQUIRED FIXES:
  - Convert every `get_manager as _manager` usage to await the coroutine before storing it (e.g., `self.manager = await _manager()` inside an async initializer or lazily via async helper).
  - Update all consumers to await manager methods (`await self.manager.spawn_shell(...)`, `await self.manager.describe(...)`, etc.). For synchronous modules such as `app/apps/terminal/backend.py`, refactor endpoints to async (or provide async wrappers) so they can await the manager.
  - Replace `anyio.to_thread.run_sync(mgr.list_shells)` and similar with direct awaits.

CONCLUSION:
The async manager integration is incomplete—large portions of the app still treat the manager synchronously, so core services (agent bridge, terminal backend, shell status) fail instantly. Must address these call sites before the refactor can be considered stable.

